flowchart TB
    subgraph vpc[Consumer VPC: conceptual only]
        subgraph aza[Availability Zone A]
            appa[Private workload A]
            rta[Associated route table A]
            enia[Interface endpoint ENI A]
        end

        subgraph azb[Availability Zone B]
            appb[Private workload B]
            rtb[Associated route table B]
            enib[Interface endpoint ENI B]
        end

        gateway[Gateway endpoint: S3 or DynamoDB\nroute target for AWS-managed prefix list]
        epSG[Interface-endpoint security group\nallow required listener traffic from workload security group]
        dns[VPC DNS\nprivate DNS only where the selected interface service supports it]
        policy[Endpoint policy, if supported\nadditional endpoint-use guardrail]
    end

    s3[S3 or DynamoDB\nsame-Region service]
    supported[Supported AWS service or\npublished endpoint service]
    nat[NAT Gateway\nonly for required unsupported IPv4 egress]

    appa --> rta
    appb --> rtb
    rta -->|S3/DynamoDB prefix-list route| gateway
    rtb -->|S3/DynamoDB prefix-list route| gateway
    gateway -->|same-Region VPC traffic| s3

    appa -->|service DNS query| dns
    appb -->|service DNS query| dns
    dns -->|private endpoint IPs or endpoint-specific name| enia
    dns -->|private endpoint IPs or endpoint-specific name| enib
    enia --> epSG
    enib --> epSG
    epSG -->|PrivateLink traffic| supported
    policy --- supported

    rta -. only when a narrower path cannot serve the destination .-> nat
    rtb -. only when a narrower path cannot serve the destination .-> nat

    costs[Cost comparison, not a price quote\nGateway: no additional endpoint charge\nInterface: endpoint type x selected AZ hours + GB processed\nNAT: NAT-AZ hours + GB processed + applicable transfer]
    gateway --- costs
    enia --- costs
    nat --- costs

    boundary[Gateway: S3/DynamoDB only; route-table association; no on-premises, TGW, or peered-VPC extension\nInterface: one ENI per selected AZ; service support, DNS, security group, and endpoint-policy behavior vary by service\nRoutes choose a path; IAM and service resource policies must also allow access]
    policy --- boundary
